{
  "title": "Fracture Healing",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/9009/fracture-healing",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 12 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Introduction",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Fracture healing involves a complex and sequential set of events to restore injured bone to pre-fracture condition",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "stem cells are crucial to the fracture repair process",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "periosteum and endosteum are the two major sources",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Fracture stability dictates the type of healing that will occur",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanical stability governs the mechanical strain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "when the strain is below 2%, primary bone healing will occur",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "when the strain is between 2% and 10%, secondary bone healing will occur",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Modes of bone healing",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "primary bone healing (strain is < 2%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**intramembranous healing**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "occurs via **Haversian remodeling**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**occurs with absolute stability constructs**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "secondary bone healing (strain is between 2%-10%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "involves responses in the periosteum and external soft tissues.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "endochondral healing",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "occurs with non-rigid fixation, as fracture braces, external fixation, bridge plating, intramedullary nailing, etc.",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "bone healing may occur as a combination of the above two process depending on the stability throughout the construct",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 3,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Type of Fracture Healing with Treatment Technique**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Cast treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Secondary: endochondral ossification",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "External fixation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Secondary: endochondral ossification",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "IM nailing",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Secondary: endochondral ossification",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Compression plate",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Primary: Haversian remodeling",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Secondary Bone Healing",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 3,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Stages of Fracture Healing**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Inflammation**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Hematoma forms and provides a source of hematopoietic cells capable of secreting growth factors.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Macrophages, neutrophils, and platelets release several cytokines",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "this includes PDGF, TNF-Alpha, TGF-Beta, IL-1,6, 10,12",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "they may be detected as early as 24 hours post-injury",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "lack of TNF-Alpha (ie. HIV) results in delay of both endochondral/ intramembranous ossification",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "BMPs, fibroblasts and mesenchymal cells migrate to fracture site and granulation tissue forms around fracture ends",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "During fracture healing granulation tissue tolerates the greatest strain before failure",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Osteoblasts and fibroblasts proliferate",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Inhibition of COX-2 (ie NSAIDs) causes repression of runx-2/osterix, which are critical for differentiation of osteoblastic cells",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Repair**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Primary callus forms within two weeks. If the bone ends are not touching, then bridging soft callus forms.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "The mechanical environment drives differentiation of either osteoblastic (stable enviroment) or chondryocytic (unstable environment) lineages of cells",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Endochondral ossification converts soft callus to hard callus (woven bone).",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Medullary callus also supplements the bridging soft callus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Cytokines drive chondocytic differentiation.",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Cartilage production provides provisional stabilization",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Type II collagen (cartilage) is produced early in fracture healing and then followed by type I collagen (bone) expression",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Amount of callus is inversely proportional to extent of immobilization",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Primary cortical healing occurs with rigid immobilization (ie. compression plating)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Endochondral healing with periosteal bridging occurs with closed treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Remodeling**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Begins in middle of repair phase and continues long after clinical union",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Chondrocytes undergo terminal differentiation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Complex interplay of signaling pathways including, indian hedgehog (Ihh), parathyroid hormone-related peptide (PTHrP), FGF and BMP",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "These molecules are also involved in terminal differentiation of the appendicular skeleton",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**Type X collagen** types is expressed by hypertrophic chondrocytes as the extraarticular matrix undergoes calcification",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Proteases degrade the extracellular matrix",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Cartilaginous calcification takes place at the junction between the maturing chondrocytes and newly forming bone",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Multiple factors are expressed as bone is formed including TGF-Betas, IGFs, osteocalcin, collagen I, V and XI",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Subsequently, chondrocytes become apoptotic and VEGF production leads to new vessel invasion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Newly formed bone (woven bone) is remodeling via organized osteoblastic/osteoclastic activity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Shaped through",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**Wolff's law:** bone remodels in response to mechanical stress",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**Piezoelectric charges**: bone remodels is response to electric charges: compression side is electronegative and stimulates osteoblast formation, tension side is electropostive and simulates osteoclasts",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Variables that Influence Fracture Healing",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Internal variables",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "blood supply (most important)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "initially the blood flow decreases with vascular disruption",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "after few hours to days, the blood flow increases",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "this peaks at 2 weeks and normalizes at 3-5 months",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "un-reamed nails maintain the endosteal blood supply",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "reaming compromises of the inner 50-80% of the cortex",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "looser fitting nails allow more quick reperfusion of the endosteal blood supply versus canal filling nails",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "head injury may increase osteogenic response",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "mechanical factors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "bony soft tissue attachments",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "mechanical stability/strain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "location of injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "degree of bone loss",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "pattern (segmental or fractures with butterfly fragments)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "increased risk of nonunion likely secondary to compromise of the blood supply to the intercalary segment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "External variables",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Low Intensity Pulsed Ultrasound (LIPUS)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "exact mechanism for enhancement of fracture healing is not clear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "alteration of protein expression",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "elevation of vascularity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "development of mechanical strain gradient",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "accelerates fracture healing and increases mechanical strength of callus (including torque and stiffness)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "the beneficial ultrasound signal is 30 mW/cm2 pulsed-wave",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "healing rates for delayed unions/nonunions has been reported to be close to 80%",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "bone stimulators",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "four main delivery modes of electrical stimulation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "direct current",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "decrease osteoclast activity and increase osteoblast activity by reducing oxygen concentration and increasing local tissue pH",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "capacitively coupled electrical fields (alternating current, AC)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "affect synthesis of cAMP, collagen and calcification of carilage",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "pulsed electromagnetic fields",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "cause calcification of fibrocartilage",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "combined magnetic fields",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "they lead to elevated concentrations of TGF-Beta and BMP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "COX-2",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "promotes fracture healing by causing mesenchymal stem cells to differentiate into osteoblasts",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "radiation (high dose)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "long term changes within the remodeling systems",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cellularity is diminished",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Patient factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "diet",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "nutritional deficiencies",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "vitamin D and calcium",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "as high as 84% of patients with nonunion were found to have metabolic issues",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "greater than 66% of these patients had vitamin D deficiencies",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "in a rat fracture model",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "protein malnourishment decreases fracture callus strength",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "amino acid supplementation increases muscle protein content and fracture callus mineralization",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "gastric bypass patients",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "calcium absorption is affected because of duodenal bypass with Roux-en-Y procedure",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "leads to decreased Ca/Vit D levels, hyperparathyroidism (secondary) & increased Ca resportion from bone",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "treat these patients with Ca/Vit D supplementation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "gastric banding does not lead to these abnormalities because the duodenum is not bypassed",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "diabetes mellitus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "affects the repair and remodeling of bone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "decreased cellularity of the fracture callus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "delayed endochondral ossification",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "diminished strength of the fracture callus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "fracture healing takes 1.6 times longer in diabetic patients versus non-diabetic patients",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "nicotine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "decreases rate of fracture healing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "inhibits growth of new blood vessels as bone is remodeled",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "increase risk of nonunion (increases risk of pseudoarthrosis in spine fusion by 500%)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "decreased strength of fracture callus",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "smokers can take ~70% longer to heal open tibial shaft fractures versus non-smokers",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "HIV",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "higher prevalence of fragility fractures with associated delayed healing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "contributing factors",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "anti-retroviral medication",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "poor intraosseous circulation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "TNF-Alpha deficiency",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "poor nutritional intake",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "medications affecting healing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "bisphosphonates are recognized as a cause of osteoporotic fractures with long term usage",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "recent studies demonstrated longer healing times for surgically treated wrist fractures in patients on bisphosphonates",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "long term usage may be associated with atypical subtrochanteric/femoral shaft fractures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "systemic corticosteroids",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "studies have shown a 6.5% higher rate of intertrochanteric fracture non unions",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "NSAIDs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "prolonged healing time becaue of COX enzyme inhbition",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "quinolones",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "toxic to chondrocytes and diminishes fracture repair",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
